| **Cross‑coupling (‑0.1 × x)** | When the cart is already displaced, a small bias in the pole term gently nudges it back toward the centre, reducing the later cart‑only correction. |
| **Tighter cart dead‑zone (0.04 m / 0.04 m/s)** | The cart is kept nearer to the centre, which in turn reduces the torque on the pole caused by large cart excursions. |
| **Slightly larger cart gains (0.7 × x, 0.6 × ẋ)** | Once the cart drifts, the controller reacts faster, preventing the pole from being “dragged” by a far‑away cart. |
| **Same saturation logic** | Guarantees the action stays within the allowed ‑3 N … +3 N range. |

