| **Reduced `k_x` / `k_xdot` (0.6 / 0.5)** | Cart‑position correction is still present (prevents the cart from drifting to the edge) but is not so strong that it steals force from pole‑stabilisation. |
| **Dead‑zone (θ < 0.003 rad, θ̇ < 0.006 rad/s)** | Removes unnecessary jitter when the pole is already within the tolerance, saving the limited force budget for when it is really needed. |
| **Angle‑dependent scaling (α = 1.5)** | When the pole is already leaning (|θ| ≈ 0.1 rad) the controller automatically amplifies its output, preventing the pole from “creeping” toward the failure angle. |
| **Bias (0.012 N)** | A tiny nudge that eliminates the symmetric dead‑zone that sometimes caused the controller to hover around 0 N while the pole was still drifting. |
| **Hard clipping** | Guarantees the full ±3 N are available instantly; no smooth‑saturation delay as with tanh. |

