| Component | Reason |
|-----------|--------|
| **Dead‑zone (|θ| < 0.002, |θ̇| < 0.004)** | Removes unnecessary jitter when the pole is already stable. |
| **Higher PD gains (Kp = 6, Kd = 2.5)** | Gives a stronger torque about the pivot, allowing the pole to be pulled back before it reaches the ±0.2 rad limit. |
| **Small cart‑feedback (Kx, Kv)** | Prevents the cart from drifting far from the centre, which otherwise would reduce the effectiveness of the pole term. |
| **Adaptive scaling (up to 2.2)** | When the pole is far from vertical the controller automatically amplifies the command, delivering near‑maximum force when it is most needed. |
| **Symmetry‑breaking bias (0.002 < |θ| < 0.018)** | Avoids the “dead‑lock” where the PD term is almost zero and the controller hesitates to choose a direction. |
| **Saturation** | Guarantees the output respects the physical limits (‑3 N … +3 N). |

