|--------|--------|
| **Higher Kp / Kd (8.5 / 3.2)** | Gives a stronger corrective torque; the pole can be pulled back even when it has already acquired a noticeable angular velocity. |
| **Cart terms (Kx = 0.55, Kv = 0.38)** | Gently nudges the cart toward the centre, preventing the cart from “running away” and making later corrections easier. |
| **Scale factor up to 2.5** | Allows the controller to use the full 3 N thrust when the pole is close to the failure angle, dramatically reducing the chance of a sudden crash. |
| **Dead‑zone tightened to |θ|<0.002 & |θ̇|<0.004 plus cart near‑zero** | Removes the jitter that was observed in the previous version when the pole hovered around 0.001 rad but the cart was already moving. |
| **Bias of +0.010 · sign(θ)** | Slightly larger than the previous 0.008; this “kick” reliably pushes the pole out of the tiny dead‑zone without causing overshoot. |
| **Safety check unchanged** | Guarantees we never output NaN/Inf forces. |

