|--------------|-----------------|
| **Stronger cart‑centering gains** (`K_x = -0.9`, `K_xdot = -0.8`) | The cart is pulled back toward the centre much faster, preventing the slow drift that previously caused the pole to fall when the cart reached the track edge. |
| **Scaling factor capped at 2.0** (instead of 1.5) | When the pole is already tilted (|θ|≈0.15 rad) the controller can apply up to ~ 30 % more corrective torque, which delays the inevitable fall and gives the cart‑centering term time to act. |
| **Larger proportional bias (0.04·sign(θ))** for tiny angles | The bias is now comparable to the cart‑term when the pole is almost upright, so the controller starts nudging the cart back before the drift becomes large. |
| **Tanh saturation** | Guarantees a smooth transition to the force limits, avoiding sudden jumps that could destabilise the pole. |
| **Retained dead‑zone** | Prevents high‑frequency chatter when the system is already balanced. |

