| • Checking for non‑finite values (safety) | – |

**3. New strategy (the one we will adopt)**  

```text
# -------------------------------------------------
#  Pole‑Cart Linear‑Quadratic controller with
#  angle‑dependent gain and smooth saturation.
# -------------------------------------------------

IF NOT finite(x) OR NOT finite(xdot) OR NOT finite(theta) OR NOT finite(thetad)
    force ← 0.0
ELSE IF |theta| > 0.20                     # failure region – stop pushing
    force ← 0.0
ELSE
    # ---- 1. Base linear feedback -----------------
    #   pole terms (dominant)
    pole_term   ← 3.5 * theta + 2.0 * thetad

    #   cart terms (stronger than before)
    cart_term   ← 0.6 * x + 0.8 * xdot

    raw_force   ← pole_term - cart_term

    # ---- 2. Angle‑dependent scaling ---------------
    #   give more authority when the pole is farther away
    scale ← 1.0 + 2.2 * MIN(|theta|, 0.20)   # 1 … 1+2.2*0.20 = 1.44
    raw_force ← raw_force * scale

    # ---- 3. Soft saturation (tanh) ---------------
    #   keeps the output smooth and respects the ±3 N limit
    force_raw ← 3.0 * tanh(raw_force / 3.0)

    # ---- 4. Final clipping (safety) ---------------
    IF force_raw > 3.0   THEN force ← 3.0
    ELSE IF force_raw < -3.0 THEN force ← -3.0
    ELSE force ← force_raw
    ENDIF
ENDIF
```

