### 2. Revised strategy (the one we will adopt)

Below is a compact pseudo‑code that incorporates the lessons above.  
All constants were tuned by hand on the logged data; they can be fine‑tuned further with a short grid‑search if needed.

```text
# --------------------------------------------------------------
#  Pole‑Balancing Controller – “Light‑Cart, Scaled‑PD + Damping”
# --------------------------------------------------------------

IF NOT finite(x) OR NOT finite(xdot) OR NOT finite(theta) OR NOT finite(thetad)
    force ← 0.0                                 # safety guard
ELSE IF |theta| > 0.20
    force ← 0.0                                 # episode already failed
ELSE
    # ---- 1.  Dead‑zone (no actuation when truly upright) ----
    IF |theta| < 0.003 AND |thetad| < 0.006
        force ← 0.0
    ELSE
        # ---- 2.  Scaling factor (grow with angle, but cap) ----
        scale ← 1.0 + 2.0 * MIN(|theta|, 0.20)   # 1 → 1.4 for |θ|=0.20
        IF scale > 1.5
            scale ← 1.5

        # ---- 3.  PD term for the pole ----
        pole_pd ← 3.5 * theta + 2.0 * thetad

        # ---- 4.  Light cart‑centering term ----
        cart_term ← 0.4 * x + 0.3 * xdot

        # ---- 5.  Damping on pole angular velocity (optional) ----
        #    This term reduces overshoot when the pole is swinging fast.
        damp ← -0.5 * thetad                     # negative feedback on θ̇

        # ---- 6.  Raw (un‑saturated) force ----
        raw ← scale * (pole_pd + damp - cart_term)

        # ---- 7.  Tiny bias for small non‑zero angles ----
        IF 0.003 < |theta| AND |theta| < 0.020
            raw ← raw + 0.008 * sign(theta) * scale

        # ---- 8.  Saturate with tanh (keeps us inside [-3,3]) ----
        force ← 3.0 * tanh(raw / 3.0)

        # (no extra clipping needed – tanh already respects the limits)
    ENDIF
ENDIF
```

