| Component | Change vs. S‑2 | Expected effect |
|-----------|----------------|-----------------|
| `scale` (1 + 2.5·|θ|, cap 1.5) | Slightly larger gain for moderate angles | Faster correction when the pole tilts, without blowing up at the limit |
| Adaptive `pole_damp` (0.5 → 0.8 when |θ| > 0.05) | More damping when the pole is far from vertical | Reduces overshoot and high‑frequency swing that caused the “spikes”. |
| Cart term only if |x| > 0.05 | Prevents unnecessary pulling when the cart is already near centre | Reduces interference with the pole PD when the cart is well‑centered, leading to smoother behaviour. |
| Bias magnitude reduced to 0.006 and gated by |θ̇| < 0.01 | Bias is now only used to overcome static friction, not to push the pole when it already moves | Eliminates the occasional overshoot that terminated episodes in S‑2. |
| No extra hard clipping after tanh | Simpler, tanh already limits the command | Keeps the controller transparent for debugging. |

