| **Edge‑repel** (`edge_repulsion`) | Prevents the cart from drifting to the hard limits, the most common failure after the pole is stable. The term is very soft (max ≈ 0.8 N) so it does not fight the pole‑PD when the pole is far from vertical. |
| **Tightened boost cap (2 N)** | Keeps the recovery boost strong enough to catch a falling pole but never large enough to overshoot the cart. |
| **Slightly higher angle gain (4.3)** | Improves the controller’s ability to correct small angular errors without relying on the boost. |
| **Slightly lower velocity gain (2.4)** | Reduces the tendency to “chase” the pole’s angular velocity, which can cause oscillations. |
| **Keep the hard‑stop rule removed** | The PD + boost + edge‑repel together keep |θ| well below 0.20 rad; the hard‑stop is unnecessary and can introduce a sudden –3 N jerk that destabilises the system. |

