| **Slightly lower velocity gain (2.4)** | Reduces the tendency to “chase” the pole’s angular velocity, which can cause oscillations. |
| **Keep the hard‑stop rule removed** | The PD + boost + edge‑repel together keep |θ| well below 0.20 rad; the hard‑stop is unnecessary and can introduce a sudden –3 N jerk that destabilises the system. |

